# Review routing for the files that define and enforce the SPARK crate's gates.
# Adapted from memcp's CODEOWNERS.
#
# A gate can be satisfied by editing what it reads: the trust gate checks that a
# justification is present, not that anyone read it, and the proof gate accepts
# whatever proof-xfail.txt allows. The GPR and alire.toml carry the committed
# proof levels and the compiler switches (a -gnatp or -gnatws there suppresses
# what the trust gate scans src/ for). These entries put a reviewer in the loop.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so general patterns come first.
# NSA's own files are not listed: this fork does not route their review.

/spark/*.gpr                                @manthonyaiello
/spark/alire.toml                           @manthonyaiello

/spark/scripts/trust-surface.txt            @manthonyaiello
/spark/scripts/check-trust-surface.sh       @manthonyaiello

/spark/scripts/proof-xfail.txt              @manthonyaiello
/spark/scripts/check-proof.sh               @manthonyaiello
/spark/scripts/prove.sh                     @manthonyaiello
/spark/scripts/board.py                     @manthonyaiello
/spark/scripts/board-rows.txt               @manthonyaiello

/spark/scripts/check-docs.sh                @manthonyaiello
/spark/scripts/check-doc-placement.sh       @manthonyaiello

/.github/workflows/spark-*.yml              @manthonyaiello
/.github/actions/setup-alire-spark/         @manthonyaiello
/.github/CODEOWNERS                         @manthonyaiello
